    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1196">

                <pb facs="0967" n="851" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg851"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/6958.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Mr.
                            Parker, representing American
                        interests</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 26, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>141. American settlers in Yaqui Valley, Sonora, complain of inadequate protection
                    against Indians. Urge appropriate authorities to issue orders immediately to
                    General Dieguez to send at least three hundred soldiers to Yaqui Valley.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
